#
# Competency (the GOVERNING question): a computed feature is a math:LocalSection and is a
# global truth ONLY when it extends to a math:GlobalSection (H⁰) AND discharges the H¹
# math:GluingObstruction. This query returns each gmeow:TopologyClaim with its local section,
# the global section it extends to, and the discharged obstruction — so a claim asserting
# global truth appears ONLY with both the extension and the discharge present. Over the
# worked example this is exactly one row; a raw local feature with no extension/discharge
# would not appear, which is the point.
PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>
SELECT ?claim ?localSection ?globalSection ?obstruction WHERE {
    ?claim a gmeow:TopologyClaim ;
        gmeow:claimLocalSection ?localSection ;
        gmeow:extendsToGlobalSection ?globalSection ;
        gmeow:dischargesObstruction ?obstruction .
}
ORDER BY ?claim
